        <!-- Module 2: Export & Import -->
        <section id="module2" class="module-2">
            <h2 class="module-title">2. Exporting from Blender & Importing into Godot</h2>
            <p>Use glTF 2.0 embedded exports to transfer your scene, animations and camera from Blender into Godot. These steps help preserve animations and keep file sizes manageable.</p>
            <ol class="steps">
                <li><strong>Organize your animation in Blender:</strong> In the NLA editor, push each animation action down to NLA strips and name them clearly. Clean up unused keyframes and apply transforms to ensure proper export【126456036935714†L68-L90】.</li>
                <li><strong>Export as glTF 2.0 (embedded):</strong> In Blender, go to <em>File &gt; Export &gt; glTF 2.0</em>. Choose <em>glTF Embedded (.gltf)</em>, enable <em>Selected Objects</em>, enable <em>NLA Strips</em>, and disable <em>Export all animation actions</em> to prevent extra data【126456036935714†L98-L106】.</li>
                <li><strong>Include camera and lights:</strong> Select your camera and any lights you want to transfer. The exported glTF will include these objects and their animations.</li>
                <li><strong>Import into Godot:</strong> Drag the <code>.gltf</code> file into the Godot project. Godot automatically creates a scene with your meshes, materials, camera and animations. You may need to rename nodes or set the AnimationPlayer’s <em>root node</em> to match your new scene hierarchy if the imported camera animation doesn’t play【211856862347448†L57-L64】.</li>
                <li><strong>Verify animations:</strong> Open the imported scene, press play on the AnimationPlayer and confirm that your camera, characters and objects animate as expected【126456036935714†L114-L124】【126456036935714†L131-L139】.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="resources">
                <h3>Resources</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="https://supermatrix.dev/fix-your-broken-blender-to-godot-animation-exports" target="_blank">Supermatrix – Fix your broken Blender to Godot animation exports (2026)</a> – detailed NLA export guide【126456036935714†L68-L90】.</li>
                    <li><a href="https://www.khronos.org/assets/uploads/developers/library/2023-godot-pcvr-openxr-tutorial.pdf" target="_blank">Khronos – Godot PCVR OpenXR Tutorial (PDF)</a> – glTF import details and OpenXR setup【2569936289947†L49-L113】.</li>
                    <li><a href="https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/export/exporting_glTF_scenes_from_blender.html" target="_blank">Godot Documentation – Exporting glTF scenes from Blender</a>.</li>
