        <!-- Module 4: VR Setup & Yaw Integration -->
        <section id="module4" class="module-4">
            <h2 class="module-title">4. VR Setup and Yaw VR Integration</h2>
            <p>This module explains how to set up a VR experience in Godot using OpenXR. It also introduces Yaw VR simulators for motion feedback.</p>
            <ol class="steps">
                <li><strong>Configure OpenXR:</strong> Install Godot’s OpenXR plugin and enable XR settings in your project. In the project settings, enable <em>XR Features > OpenXR</em>. Ensure your default OpenXR runtime (e.g., SteamVR for HTC Vive) is selected in the headset’s software【2569936289947†L49-L113】.</li>
                <li><strong>Create an XR rig:</strong> Add an <em>XROrigin3D</em> node to your scene. As children, add an <em>XRCamera3D</em> and two <em>XRController3D</em> nodes (for left and right hands). Position them at the player’s starting point【2569936289947†L49-L113】.</li>
                <li><strong>Visualize controllers:</strong> Add <em>MeshInstance3D</em> nodes as children of the XRController nodes to display virtual hands or controllers. Use simple shapes during development to test placement【2569936289947†L49-L113】.</li>
                <li><strong>Add an environment and floor:</strong> Include ground geometry or a plane so the player can see the floor. Use the environment settings from Module 3 for realistic lighting.</li>
                <li><strong>Set up input actions:</strong> Configure input mappings for VR actions (grab, teleport, interact) under <em>Project Settings > Input Map</em>. Use Godot’s XR input functions to handle controller buttons and analog axes.</li>
                <li><strong>Connect the Yaw VR simulator (optional):</strong> To add motion feedback, use the <a href="https://docs.yawvr.com/software/gamelink" target="_blank">Yaw Game Link tool</a>. Power on the simulator, open Game Link, connect to your simulator, select your game/application, and configure motion strength and vibration settings【710468388657595†L71-L100】. Game Link supports many VR games and is free to use【710468388657595†L91-L102】.</li>
                <li><strong>Advanced Yaw integration:</strong> For deeper integration, use the <a href="https://docs.yawvr.com/sdk" target="_blank">Yaw SDK</a>. It allows direct communication with the simulator through C++, C# or Python, enabling real‑time control across platforms【826213767624787†L55-L82】. However, Godot doesn’t have a native plugin yet, so you may need to build a GDExtension to interface with the C API.</li>
            </ol>
