        <!-- Module 5: Expanding Ideas -->
        <section id="module5" class="module-5">
            <h2 class="module-title">5. Expanding Ideas & Next Steps</h2>
            <p>Now that you know how to build a cinematic and bring it into Godot with VR, consider these ideas to push your project further.</p>
            <ol class="steps">
                <li><strong>Add interactivity:</strong> Incorporate interactable elements like control panels or weapons by scripting XR controller inputs. Use Godot’s physics engine to enable collisions and responses.</li>
                <li><strong>Hand‑tracking and physics:</strong> Use the XR Tools plugin to enable direct hand tracking for headsets that support it, or connect additional controllers like hand sets for more immersive interactions.</li>
                <li><strong>Multi‑user experiences:</strong> Explore networking through Godot’s High‑Level Multiplayer API to allow multiple users to view or interact with the same cinematic in real time.</li>
                <li><strong>Integration with motion platforms:</strong> Build a custom GDExtension using the Yaw SDK to control the motion simulator directly from Godot. This requires programming but allows you to synchronize motion with the camera for full immersion.</li>
                <li><strong>Use other game engines:</strong> Unreal and Unity have ready‑made Yaw SDK plugins. If you need advanced features unavailable in Godot, consider building the VR experience in one of these engines.</li>
                <li><strong>Create an educational series:</strong> Turn your cinematic workflow into a class project. Divide tasks among students: modelling, texturing, animation, VR setup, and documentation. Use this workbook as a starting point.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="resources">
                <h3>Resources</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><a href="https://www.godotengine.org/asset-library/tag/openxr" target="_blank">Godot Asset Library – XR Tools</a> – to add hand tracking and teleports.</li>
